Additional Rules
Defensive Roles: There are some defensive roles (i.e. Runner, Scared Werewolf) that require the Host to be aware of their identity. In these cases, the Host can either choose to check cards at the start of the game, discretly check cards of players that may die at the end of night, before waking town, or waking up the defensive roles in Night 1 to check (and remember) their identity.

Role Change: There are some roles that can cause role changes. When playing with one of these roles you can choose one of the following: have each player check their own card each morning; or, wake up players to inform them of their role changes. To do this you must wake some roles specifically (i.e. Apprentice, Cursed Civilian), some roles that are unaware of being a role change's target by e.g. touching their shoulder (i.e. Infecting Werewolf, Vampire, Thief) and some roles need to specifically be informed (i.e. Gallant Fox, Mystic Fox). Players should learn this info at the end of night/start of day.
